idth:100%"><p>Most people probably know creatine as a supplement to improve body composition and fitness performance - this is true and supported by a large number of studies.</p><br><p>What many don't know is that creatine may have further positive mental benefits. Creatine fuels ATP production in the brain, <strong>improving memory, focus, and mental clarity</strong> - particularly under stress or sleep deprivation.</p><p><br></p><p>Early studies are also beginning to show <strong>broader neuroprotective benefits</strong> with high levels of creatine supplementation that cross the brain-blood barrier.</p><p><br></p><p>That means that not only can creatine benefit you today, you're also doing your future self a favor.</p><br></span></div></div><picture data-rid="dccad0e1-cb87-4830-befd-a119ab9d5a82" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-asorzl"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PerformanceUnderSleepDeprivation_BeigeBG_1a5d7e45-713b-4502-a679-726daaad198b.png?v=1741021859&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PerformanceUnderSleepDeprivation_BeigeBG_1a5d7e45-713b-4502-a679-726daaad198b.png?v=1741021859&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PerformanceUnderSleepDeprivation_BeigeBG_1a5d7e45-713b-4502-a679-726daaad198b.png?v=1741021859&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PerformanceUnderSleepDeprivation_BeigeBG_1a5d7e45-713b-4502-a679-726daaad198b.png?v=1741021859" alt="Graph of cognitive performance under sleep deprivation, comparing creatine and placebo groups over 8 hours." class="r-uuff7q" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="8edec9f3-6ab9-49bc-bb6b-370b2edfeb63" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.